    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 81.88 efficiency score makes him our premier start. Facing a soft matchup against Aaron Civale (4.52 xERA) with the added benefit of wind blowing out, **Gunnar Henderson** is perfectly positioned to capitalize on his elite base projection and favorable order placement. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** (75.90) and **Jackson Merrill** (74.04) represent high-leverage plays; **Kyle Tucker** enjoys a significant skill-based advantage against Spencer Strider, while **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a strong platoon advantage despite the potential for an elite hold from the opposing bullpen. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains an essential pivot with a 73.10 score, providing high-volume offensive upside against the highly vulnerable Kochanowicz.\n\nSeveral players are benefiting from structural boosts, most notably **Coby Mayo** (61.69) and **Jacob Wilson** (64.14), who both capitalize on significant park factor adjustments and wind conditions that elevate their raw projections. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (67.75) continues to be a core contributor, showing consistent efficiency against Janson Junk, while **Sam Antonacci** (60.70) remains a lock in the outfield due to an impressive 0.398 xwOBA that justifies his status despite a slight park penalty. We are monitoring the status of **Drake Baldwin**, **Liam Hicks**, **Coby Mayo**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jackson Merrill** closely, as their scores are currently tethered to projected order assumptions; any downward shifts in their batting slots could necessitate a recalibration of our exposure.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Nolan Schanuel** (53.01), who finished just shy of the lineup threshold. While he offers a respectable floor against Yesavage, he was ultimately bypassed in favor of **Josh Lowe** (57.15), whose dynamic platoon advantage provides a higher categorical ceiling for our 5x5 objectives. While **Miguel Vargas** and **Josh Jung** remained in the conversation, the volatility of their respective matchups and lower aggregate efficiency scores kept them on the sidelines. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Josh Lowe**, as his #9 spot in the order slightly hinders his runs-scored potential, but we remain confident that the aggressive stacking of high-efficiency hitters provides the best path to maximizing our daily performance.",
